box(70,318,160,'Researcher','Question + judgment');box(490,254,220,'Coordinator','Plans and delegates','#e1d3ed');box(295,363,175,'Literature','Retrieve + verify');box(510,363,175,'Analysis','Code + write');box(725,363,190,'Review','Challenge + check');box(345,485,515,'Shared workspace and progress record','Papers, results, decisions and unfinished tasks','#e1d3ed');box(1015,318,190,'Research files','Data · code · PDF');para(70,603,'The harness manages execution around the model. The researcher remains part of the revision loop.',1120,22);link(70,658,'Open the four-stage interactive diagram','/#8',18);text(630,658,'Teaching schematic; no agents are running on the slide.',17,color='#555555');end('In the browser, click the stages: assignment, parallel work, cross-checking, revision. Explain harness once as the software around the model that handles tools, state and execution. Saved project files allow continuation beyond one conversation window. This schematic combines common architectural patterns; it is not a faithful diagram of one vendor product. Agent agreement still needs source and substantive checks.')
frame(2,'1. Complete cognitive offloading');bullets(['Give it a bounded task and inspect what comes back.','“Reproduce this figure from the supplied data and document any discrepancies.”','Other uses: bibliographic records, file conversion, replication checks.'],gap=105);para(70,558,'The failure is accepting an output because it looks finished.',1100,24);end('1:00–2:00. Here the researcher specifies a task with a checkable result. Execution can be delegated, but responsibility for the result remains with us. An example is reproducing a figure: compare data, axes, values and exclusions, rather than just seeing that an image appeared. This is one working relationship, not the lowest rung of a hierarchy.')
frame(3,'2. Guided collaboration');bullets(['Let it do much of the work; intervene where a decision matters.','“Show me the proposed measures before running the analysis.”','Other uses: developing an analysis, revising a coding scheme, comparing operationalizations.'],gap=105);para(70,566,'The failure is approving each step without really examining it.',1100,24);end('2:00–3:00. The point is to put review at a consequential choice. Asking to see measures before analysis is useful; asking it to report every trivial step is usually not. We can give reasons for a change and have it follow the implications through code, tables and writing. We should inspect the revised result, not just the acknowledgement.')
frame(4,'3. The pain-in-the-ass coauthor');para(70,205,'You bring an argument. It questions it. You respond, and work through the implications together.',1100,30);para(70,342,'“I think these findings support displacement. Here is why.<br/>What am I missing?”',1100,28);para(70,480,'Useful for theory, measurement, identification and interpretation.<br/>Its objections need scrutiny too; it can misunderstand the evidence.',1100,25);end('3:00–4:00. This is a paired intellectual relationship, not outsourcing a referee report. You explain your interpretation; it raises a problem; you answer; the project changes through the exchange. The third mode describes an intellectual role, while the first two emphasize delegation. We can move among all three during the same project. AI objections can be wrong, and agreement is not a validation test.')
frame(5,'Do chatbots change how people seek support?');C.drawImage(str(P/'article-headline.png'),70,H-310,width=1060,height=142.4375,mask='auto');text(70,347,'Rachel Hall, The Guardian, 25 March 2025',19,color='#555555');para(70,402,'Our question: do AI chatbots reduce requests for support<br/>from friends and family?',1110,31);para(70,493,'An agent can find papers, compare findings, check citations and write a synthesis.',1110,23);link(70,577,'Open the article','https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/mar/25/heavy-chatgpt-users-tend-to-be-more-lonely-suggests-research');end('4:00–5:00. The headline is a cropped screenshot of the actual article. Use this question to introduce what an agent-assisted research workflow can do: find papers, compare findings, check citations and write a synthesis. We steer the search, question its interpretation and ask it to revise. This slide introduces the demonstration, not a full research design. Open the article briefly if useful, then move to the research folder.')
frame(6,'What would you actually type?');para(70,195,'Open a project folder, add the skill, then give it the question.',1120,27);text(70,286,'Codex CLI / IDE:  $literature-audit',25);text(70,331,'Claude Code:       /literature-audit',25);text(70,369,'Header example: allowed-tools: Read WebSearch Bash(pdftotext *)',18,color='#6c567b');para(70,390,'“Find primary studies. Check the outcome instruments and source versions. Write an evidence table and bibliography. Ask me about consequential ambiguities.”',1110,27);text(70,530,'Agent → Python script → Literature database → Records to inspect',21,color='#6c567b');text(70,558,'Illustrative workflow; no script execution is claimed.',15,color='#555555');link(70,586,'Open the skill and setup instructions','/workshop/howto.html');text(70,637,'Workshop-authored skill; search and file tools depend on the session.',17,color='#555555');end('5:00–6:15. Open the how-to page. Click SKILL.md and show that it is a readable instruction file. Explain the project paths: .agents/skills in Codex, .claude/skills in Claude Code. Show the exact invocation and prompt. Click Run a script to explain the illustrative workflow: an agent calls Python, the script queries a literature API and saves records, then the agent reads and checks the returned material. The command is a teaching example; that script is not included or claimed to have run. The skill codifies the original workflow; do not imply the original review was produced by a recorded run of this skill. The local Claude login expired and the Codex CLI binary was unavailable, so no authentic skill-invocation clip is included. Official setup links are on the page. Keep this explanation practical.')
